we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{y}$, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{y}} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{x \\cdot \\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{y} \\cdot \\sqrt{y}} &=  \\\\\n(x\\sqrt{y})/(2(\\sqrt{y})^{2}) &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{x\\sqrt{y}}{2y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535582 17592186045417 false] [17592186078342 1074 "We need to remove the radical $\\sqrt{y}$ from the denominator. To do this, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{y},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{y}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x\\cdot \\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\sqrt{y}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x\\sqrt{y}}{2(\\sqrt{y})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x\\sqrt{y}}{2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078403 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519589 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078420 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519527 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078420 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519574 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078421 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519560 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078422 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519579 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078422 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519586 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078423 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519529 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078423 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519564 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078423 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519575 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078424 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519596 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078424 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519606 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078463 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519566 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078464 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519562 13194139535582 17592186045417 true] [17592186078464 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519600 13194139535582 17592186045